namespace fly.runtime

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Fly runtime — Windows (x64) backend, over Win32 (kernel32) + UCRT (Rust-style
// FFI). Ported from fly/runtime/platform/Windows/*.c. On x64 __stdcall == the
// default convention, so the symbols link undecorated.
//
// NOTE: written and compile-checked on Linux; NOT linked or run on Windows (no
// SDK/toolchain here). Two families cannot be ported faithfully because Fly has
// no working global/static storage (static class fields miscompile):
//   • Directory enumeration (fs_getdents) — the C runtime maps virtual dir-fds to
//     FindFirstFile state via a `static DirCtx s_dirs[16]` table. Without static
//     state there is no int-fd → 64-bit-handle mapping, so directory LISTING is
//     UNSUPPORTED here (fs_getdents returns -1; fs_open on a directory returns -1
//     via _open). Regular-file I/O and stat are unaffected.
//   • env_args — the C uses g_argc/g_argv (set by env_init). Here they are
//     recovered statelessly from GetCommandLineA() with a simple quote-aware split.
// Windows specifics vs POSIX: _open flag values differ (translated); stat via
// GetFileAttributesExA (fabricated POSIX mode); time via FILETIME/QPC; futex via
// WaitOnAddress/WakeByAddress; threads via CreateThread. Linked -lkernel32
// -lsynchronization (+ UCRT).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

